# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 03: MISSED CALL DETAIL

**Route:** `/mctb/missed-calls/[id]`  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-03-MISSED-CALL-DETAIL.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–02 + `transovo-mctb-page-build-specs.mdc`  
**Visual baseline:** Finished Appointment detail page screenshots

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** Missed Call Detail (`/mctb/missed-calls/[id]`, legacy `/voice/missed-calls/[id]`).

## Primary job

Authoritative record of **one** missed-call recovery event — complete lifecycle story + correct next action. Not Conversations inbox, Consent Log, Voicemail inbox, or Setup editor.

## Page structure

1. ← Missed Calls (restore list context)
2. H1: caller name or phone + missed metadata
3. One primary status + one dominant action (state-dependent)
4. Lifecycle summary: Call → Consent → Compliance text → Recovery text → Reply
5. Sections: Call details | Consent | Text-back | Conversation | Voicemail | Request form | Link activity
6. Recovery timeline (`<ol>`, authoritative events)
7. Diagnostics (collapsed, no secrets)

## Press-1 vs existing consent

- **Press-1:** separate compliance confirmation + recovery message states/content
- **Existing consent:** no Press-1 prompt/audio; factual mode language
- Never collapse two outbound messages into one generic "First text"

## Header actions (real only)

Open conversation | Call customer | View consent record | Fix setup (if actionable) — no Resend, override opt-out, force consent, fake retry

## Terminology

Caller | Business line | Text-back sender — Suppressed ≠ Failed; Delivered ≠ Sent

## States required

Loading (skeleton) | Not found | Unauthorized | Error + Retry | Partial degradation | Needs attention banner | Healthy quiet (Recovered)

## Prohibited

- Duplicate thread editor, consent dump, full voicemail player fork
- Frontend-inferred timeline from timestamps
- Fabricated failure reasons; legal guarantee copy
- Merging repeat calls into one record

## Definition of done

See full spec §71 checklist before marking detail route complete.

